    "evaluation.title": "Overview",
    "evaluation.intro": "<b>All our experiments are based on Fish S2 Pro.</b><br/>6 voices × 20 lines × joy, anger, sadness and surprise, for 480 clips. All models use the same reference audio and scoring procedure. Emotion accuracy is judged by two classifiers: emo2vec large (open source, not used in our training) and EmoRuler (our fine-tuned emo2vec large).<br/>Fish Audio Drama 3 uses the same bracketed emotion tags, which it treats as natural-language instructions. Of 720 clips, 7 stopped mid-sentence and remained silent until the 95-second limit; they were scored as generated.<br/><b>We also tested well-known multilingual TTS models, including Qwen3-TTS, OmniVoice and Ming 3.0 TTS. They work well in Chinese and English, but we heard more pronunciation errors and less natural delivery in Japanese, so this table compares models that performed better in Japanese.</b>",
